.TH "MAKE:MODULE" 1 "October 2026" "SPP Framework" "SPP Commands Manual"
.SH NAME
make:module \- Scaffold a new modern SPP module with declarative manifests and service providers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B php spp.php make:module
\fIname\fR [\fB--scope=\fIspp|optional|contrib|app\fR] [\fB--app=\fIAppName\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBmake:module\fR creates a complete module structure adhering to the Modularity 2.0 specification.
Generated components include \fBmodule.yml\fR, declarative database schema definitions in \fBdb.yml\fR,
lifecycle bootstrap routines (\fBmodinit.php\fR, \fBinstall.php\fR, \fBuninstall.php\fR), zero-boot event
registrations (\fBevents.yml\fR), and a Dependency Injection container service provider implementing
\fB\\SPP\\Core\\Interfaces\\ServiceProviderInterface\fR.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fIname\fR
The alphanumeric internal name of the module.
.TP
\fB--scope=\fIapp|optional|contrib|spp\fR
The target directory scope. Defaults to \fBapp\fR (placed in \fIsrc/<AppName>/modules/<name>\fR).
.TP
\fB--app=\fIAppName\fR
Specify the targeted application context when scaffolding an application-level module.
.SH UNDER THE HOOD
Creates module directories, writes boilerplate manifests (\fBmodule.yml\fR, \fBdb.yml\fR, \fBevents.yml\fR),
and authors lifecycle scripts without performing immediate database mutations.
